# TypeScript / React Native / Expo Standards

## Code Style
- Write concise, technical TypeScript with accurate examples
- Use functional and declarative patterns; avoid classes
- Prefer modularization over duplication
- Descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs: `isLoading`, `hasError`, `canSubmit`
- File structure order: exported component → subcomponents → helpers → static content → types

## Naming Conventions
- Directories: lowercase with dashes (`components/auth-wizard`)
- Favor named exports for components

## TypeScript
- Use TypeScript for all code; prefer `interface` over `type`
- Avoid enums; use const maps instead
- Enable strict mode
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces

## Syntax
- Use `function` keyword for pure functions
- Avoid unnecessary curly braces in simple conditionals
- Use declarative JSX

## UI & Styling
- Use shared `constants/colors.ts` for all color values — never hardcode colors inline
- Use Flexbox + `useWindowDimensions` for responsive design
- Support dark mode via `useColorScheme`
- Use `react-native-reanimated` and `react-native-gesture-handler` for animations/gestures
- Use `expo-image` with lazy loading and WebP format

## Safe Area
- Wrap top-level screens with `SafeAreaView` from `react-native-safe-area-context`
- Never hardcode padding/margins for safe areas

## Performance
- Minimize `useState`/`useEffect`; prefer context + reducers
- Memoize with `useMemo` and `useCallback` to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- Use `expo-image` for optimized image loading

## Navigation
- Use `expo-router` for all routing (file-based, dynamic routes)
- Leverage deep linking for better engagement

## State Management
- React Context + `useReducer` for global state
- Zustand for complex state (already in project)
- Avoid excessive API calls; cache responses where possible

## Error Handling
- Handle errors at the start of functions
- Use early returns to avoid deep nesting
- Avoid unnecessary `else`; use if-return pattern

## Security
- Use `expo-secure-store` for sensitive data — never plain AsyncStorage
- HTTPS only for all API calls
- Sanitize all user inputs

## Key Conventions
1. Use `expo-constants` for environment config
2. Use `expo-permissions` for device permissions
3. Test on both iOS and Android
4. Follow Expo docs: https://docs.expo.dev/
